WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.217 --> 00:00:01.784
- Hey hey girlfriend, what's up?

00:00:01.784 --> 00:00:03.117
You wanna straw?

00:00:03.117 --> 00:00:04.867
- No, don't need one.

00:00:05.721 --> 00:00:07.396
- Sucks to suck sweetheart.

00:00:07.396 --> 00:00:08.479
Hi I'm Straw.

00:00:10.596 --> 00:00:14.937
Did you know 500 million me
are used in the US per day?

00:00:14.937 --> 00:00:17.020
Per day, Sheila, per day!

00:00:18.202 --> 00:00:20.562
I'm too small for the recycling machine,

00:00:20.562 --> 00:00:22.562
so I can't get recycled.

00:00:22.779 --> 00:00:23.612
(slurps)

00:00:23.612 --> 00:00:26.195
- Hey-ey-ey-ey, I'm Coffee Cup.

00:00:27.234 --> 00:00:29.786
Did you know that an
estimated 60 billion of me

00:00:29.786 --> 00:00:32.481
end up in landfills across the US?

00:00:32.481 --> 00:00:33.898
The US each year.

00:00:34.128 --> 00:00:35.665
(laughs)

00:00:35.665 --> 00:00:36.498
They don't know what to do with me.

00:00:36.498 --> 00:00:38.228
They don't know what to do with me.

00:00:38.228 --> 00:00:39.637
At least I'm not as bad as styrofoam.

00:00:39.637 --> 00:00:40.904
(laughs)

00:00:40.904 --> 00:00:42.987
- You actually kinda are.

00:00:43.014 --> 00:00:46.013
- Hey you might think I
have it all, you know,

00:00:46.013 --> 00:00:50.481
because I'm made of paper, and
I'm recyclable, but I'm not.

00:00:50.481 --> 00:00:53.089
Only my lid and my sleeve are recyclable

00:00:53.089 --> 00:00:56.922
because baby, the inside
of me is all plastic.

00:00:58.138 --> 00:01:00.237
Shhh! Don't tell anybody,
but tell everyone.

00:01:00.237 --> 00:01:01.629
Don't tell anybody but tell people

00:01:01.629 --> 00:01:04.572
because they're not recycling me right.

00:01:04.572 --> 00:01:06.405
- Hi, I'm Plastic Bag.

00:01:06.737 --> 00:01:07.723
(scoffs)

00:01:07.723 --> 00:01:09.854
Every year, more than a trillion of me

00:01:09.854 --> 00:01:11.306
are used and thrown away.

00:01:11.306 --> 00:01:12.613
Every year, a trillion.

00:01:12.613 --> 00:01:15.834
I mean I'm fun, listen
to me, listen to me.

00:01:15.834 --> 00:01:20.501
Each year 8 million tons of
plastic end up in the ocean.

00:01:20.662 --> 00:01:22.264
(blows raspberry)

00:01:22.264 --> 00:01:23.607
I love the ocean.

00:01:23.607 --> 00:01:26.127
I hope a fish eats me, so I
end up on your dinner table.

00:01:26.127 --> 00:01:28.083
- Hello, my name is Water Bottle.

00:01:28.083 --> 00:01:30.080
You look very thirsty, are you dehydrated.

00:01:30.080 --> 00:01:31.901
- It's a hot day, so I
could use some water.

00:01:31.901 --> 00:01:34.154
- I'm easily accessible, and
I'm not just saying that.

00:01:34.154 --> 00:01:35.601
You know globally,

00:01:35.601 --> 00:01:39.007
you humans buy a million
of me each minute.

00:01:39.007 --> 00:01:39.840
- Really?

00:01:40.240 --> 00:01:42.580
- One minute (jibberish) each minute.

00:01:42.580 --> 00:01:43.688
And guess what?

00:01:43.688 --> 00:01:47.791
Only nine percent of the
plastic produced gets recycled.

00:01:47.791 --> 00:01:48.624
(speaks foreign language)

00:01:48.624 --> 00:01:51.495
We plastics take 400 years to break down.

00:01:51.495 --> 00:01:53.984
You can never get rid of me, baby.

00:01:53.984 --> 00:01:56.151
(cackles)

00:01:56.183 --> 00:01:57.766
- Hi, I'm Take Out.

00:01:59.873 --> 00:02:02.039
If I'm covered in food grease,

00:02:02.039 --> 00:02:04.039
even when you try to recycle me,

00:02:04.039 --> 00:02:06.372
I just end up in a landfill.

00:02:06.656 --> 00:02:09.739
- What do you want me to do about it?

00:02:10.218 --> 00:02:11.385
- Wash me out.

00:02:11.816 --> 00:02:14.483
Look at this Jess; you can't recycle this.

00:02:14.483 --> 00:02:16.983
You know, the average American

00:02:17.018 --> 00:02:20.185
makes about 4.4 pounds of trash a day.

00:02:21.657 --> 00:02:24.127
They always say reduce, reuse, recycle,

00:02:24.127 --> 00:02:26.960
but don't forget about the reduce.

00:02:27.452 --> 00:02:28.760
Reduce is important.

00:02:28.760 --> 00:02:31.327
- Guess what, I'm going on
a vacation to the Galapagos.

00:02:31.327 --> 00:02:32.648
(laughs)

00:02:32.648 --> 00:02:34.714
I hope I end up in a sea turtle's nose.

00:02:34.714 --> 00:02:36.797
(slurps)

00:02:37.113 --> 00:02:39.863
(rhythmic music)

